1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:04,290
(Sheldon:)Oh, yes. But there's usually planning,
courtship, advance notice.

2
00:00:04,836 --> 00:00:09,676
You know, last time, I was able to book
a cruise to the Arctic to see a solar eclipse.

3
00:00:10,592 --> 00:00:14,092
Wait, wait. You had to leave the state
because your roommate was having sex?

4
00:00:14,263 --> 00:00:17,303
(Sheldon:)I didn't have to.
The dates just happened to coincide.

5
00:00:20,143 --> 00:00:22,183
(Penny:)So do you know who's in there?

6
00:00:23,146 --> 00:00:25,276
(Sheldon:)Well, there's Leonard.

7
00:00:28,318 --> 00:00:32,778
And he's either with Leslie Winkle
or a 1930s gangster.

8
00:00:34,825 --> 00:00:37,785
Hmm. Good for him.

9
00:00:38,120 --> 00:00:40,410
(Penny:)Good for Leonard.

10
00:00:41,498 --> 00:00:42,628
(Penny:)Okay. Night.

11
00:00:42,791 --> 00:00:44,421
No, don't. Wait, hold on.

12
00:00:44,585 --> 00:00:47,925
(Leonard(entering):)- What's the matter?
- I don't know what the protocol is here.

13
00:00:49,840 --> 00:00:51,840
Do I stay? Do I leave?

14
00:00:52,009 --> 00:00:54,719
(Sheldon:)Do I wait to greet them
with a refreshing beverage?

15
00:00:56,805 --> 00:00:58,765
(Penny:)Gee, Sheldon,
you're asking the wrong girl.

16
00:00:58,932 --> 00:01:04,022
(Penny:)I'm usually on the other side
of the tie.

